<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/9th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Fontenoy</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">841 CE</span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carolingian-civil-war">Carolingian civil war</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Fontenoy was fought in 841 CE in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burgundy">Burgundy</a> between the Carolingian emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lothair-i">Lothair I</a> and his brothers <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-the-german">Louis the German</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-the-bald">Charles the Bald</a>. Lothair was defeated in a very bloody battle. The conflict led to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-verdun">Treaty of Verdun</a> in 843, which divided the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carolingian-empire">Carolingian Empire</a> into three kingdoms.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-fontenoy.jpg" alt="Battle of Fontenoy" width="320" height="323" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Pierre L'Enfant · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pierre_Lenfant_-_La_Bataille_de_Fontenoy,_le_11_mai_1745_(Ch%C3%A2teau_de_Versailles).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
